# Secrets: the Google Fonts API key lives in .env.local (see .env.example)
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Android signing and Firebase files: never commit them (the upload key lives outside the project, in ~/keys).
android/keystore.properties
*.jks
*.keystore
*.p12
*.pem
google-services.json
# iOS: the Firebase file for the iPhone/iPad app and any Apple signing material (Xcode keeps signing in your Apple account and keychain)
GoogleService-Info.plist
*.mobileprovision
*.p8
*.cer
*.certSigningRequest
GoogleService-Info.plist

# Firebase CLI cache
.firebase/
firebase-debug.log*
firestore-debug.log
ui-debug.log

# Personal tooling (AI helpers and their settings): specific to one person's setup, never shared
.claude/
.agents/
skills-lock.json

# Translation list and language names: they come from the YouVersion API, whose terms about republishing them are unconfirmed, so they stay out of the public repo.
# Anyone with their own YouVersion key can make them: node scripts/make-translation-data.mjs (see docs/youversion.md). Without them the app lists the hand-written texts only.
src/domain/bible/catalogue.json
src/domain/bible/languageNames.json

# Phone photos for the landing page letter: they show Bible text under a license, so they live on the maintainer's machine and on the live site only (see docs/ci-cd.md)
public/landing/note/

# The maintainer's release runbooks, store listing drafts, store images and audit notes: operations material, not project documentation.
# They live on the maintainer's machine (see scripts/restore-private-files.mjs).
docs/android-release.md
docs/ios-release.md
docs/play-store-listing.md
docs/play-store-updates.md
docs/accessibility-report.md
docs/play-assets/
docs/app-store-assets/
